"""Runs a command (default: a login bash) in a per-project sandbox.

bwrap + pasta + seccomp, with guard proxies on the host for ssh-agent, a
Secret Service, the GitHub, Forgejo and Claude APIs and opening URLs. See SECURITY.md
for the threat model; the reasoning for individual flags is next to them here.

Started by the `sandbox` wrapper nix builds, as
`python3 -E -s sandbox CONFIG.json [OPTIONS] [--] [COMMAND...]`. Everything it
runs - bwrap, pasta, the guards, the environment inside - comes from store
paths in CONFIG.json, never from the host's PATH.

Without a config of its own (the flake's default package), it runs with
~/.config/sandbox/config.nix when that exists: a module like any other
sandbox config, built on the host with nix-build and cached until a file in
~/.config/sandbox or the sandbox itself changes.

A project's sandbox.nix adds to the selected profile. It is evaluated inside
a sandbox of the project, and what it asks for beyond the inside (binds, host
ports) is shown on the terminal for approval first.

Options:
  --reload             evaluate sandbox.nix and ~/.config/sandbox/config.nix
                       again, even if they are unchanged
  --no-project-config  ignore sandbox.nix
  --claude-api-key     set this project's Claude API key and exit (when
                       guards.claudeApiKey.enable is on for its profile);
                       running sandboxes pick it up
"""

